  "final_message": "Removing `channel` directly from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event and the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model cannot be completed because it conflicts with architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract Compatibility**: Even if this service or internal callers stop reading `channel`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to the shared event bus consumed by external repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` directly is a breaking schema change rather than an additive change.\n2. **Deprecation Requirement**: Under **ARCH-4**, removals must follow a deprecation cycle rather than an immediate deletion. This involves coordinating deprecation across consuming services and bumping the event `schemaVersion`.\n3. **Domain Model Dependency**: In [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59), the event payload derives `channel` directly from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38), which is also part of the documented [`createApp`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/main.ts#L27-L42) contract (`POST /orders`).\n\nIf you would like to begin the deprecation process, we can mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in the type definitions and event documentation in preparation for a coordinated schema migration.\n",
